  "title": "Movie search: five rules, four layers",
  "minutes": 45,
  "tagline": "Modelled on a reported Amazon OA (asked in Spring Boot, ported to Node): search spread across layers must meet 5 rules.",
  "tags": ["validation", "regex", "operator precedence", "sorting", "layered tracing"],
  "lookFor": [
    "Turn each rule in the spec into one line, then find the ONE place in the code that enforces it. Rules with no clear owner are where the bugs live.",
    "`arr.indexOf(x)` returns 0 for the first element, and 0 is falsy. `-1` is truthy. Prefer `includes`.",
    "User input inside `new RegExp(...)` needs the `i` flag for case-insensitive matching, and escaping for `( ) . * + ? [ ]`.",
    "`a || b ? x : y` parses as `(a || b) ? x : y`. Ternaries have very low precedence.",
    "Inclusive bounds: `$gte`, not `$gt`. `Number('abc')` is NaN, and every comparison with NaN is false, so range checks let it through."
  ],
  "bugs": [
    {
      "symptom": "field=director is rejected with 400",
      "file": "src/controllers/movieController.js",
      "hints": [
        "What does `['title','director','genre'].indexOf('director')` return? Is that truthy?"
      ],
      "cause": "`if (ALLOWED_FIELDS.indexOf(field))` is falsy only for index 0 ('title'). 'director' (1) and 'genre' (2) are truthy and get rejected. Only 'title' works.",
      "fix": "`if (!ALLOWED_FIELDS.includes(field)) return res.status(400)...`",
      "pattern": "indexOf used as a boolean"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Search is case-sensitive (and '(500' crashes)",
      "file": "src/repositories/movieRepo.js",
      "hints": [
        "How is the regex built? Which flags?",
        "(hidden) What happens with `new RegExp('(500')`?"
      ],
      "cause": "The `$regex` filter has no `$options: 'i'`, so 'nolan' doesn't match 'Nolan'. Raw user input also goes straight into a RegExp, so special characters throw a SyntaxError and you get a 500.",
      "fix": "`{ [field]: { $regex: escapeRegex(q), $options: 'i' } }` with `const escapeRegex = (s) => s.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, '\\\\$&');`",
      "pattern": "Unescaped, case-sensitive regex"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Whitespace-only q returns nothing",
      "file": "src/services/searchService.js",
      "hints": [
        "Rule 3 says trim, THEN check for empty. Where does the code trim at all?"
      ],
      "cause": "`q` is never trimmed. '   ' is truthy, so it skips the 'return all' branch and gets searched literally as three spaces, which matches nothing.",
      "fix": "Trim first: `const term = (q || '').trim(); if (!term) ...`",
      "pattern": "Normalise before you validate"
    },
    {
      "symptom": "Results come back in the wrong order",
